.TH SAFEGUARD 8 "2026-07-22" "safeguard 3.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
safeguard \- Linux security audit and whitelist controller based on eBPF/LSM
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B safeguard
.RB [ \--config
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \--version ]
.RB [ \--help ]
.sp
.B safeguard controller generate
.RB [ \--output
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ \--report
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ \--mode
.IR MODE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B safeguard
is a host security audit and control tool based on eBPF and the Linux Security Module (LSM) subsystem.
It attaches eBPF programs to kernel LSM hooks to provide real-time monitoring and enforcement of
network, file, mount, and process security events.
.sp
Each audit module supports two operational modes:
.sp
.RS 4
.TP 8
.B monitor
Log events only; no enforcement. Recommended for policy validation.
.TP
.B block
Enforce the policy: matching operations are blocked and logged. Recommended for production.
.RE
.sp
Each module supports two scope targets:
.sp
.RS 4
.TP 8
.B host
Apply restrictions globally, including host and container processes.
.TP
.B container
Apply restrictions only to container processes; host processes are unaffected.
.RE
.sp
The global policy supports two modes:
.sp
.RS 4
.TP 8
.B blacklist
(Default) Allow all except explicitly denied entries.
.TP
.B whitelist
Deny all except explicitly allowed entries. Recommended for high-security environments.
.RE
.sp
.B safeguard
must be run as root. The kernel must have BPF LSM and BTF enabled.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS "Global Options"
.TP
.BR \--config \ FILE
Path to the YAML configuration file. Default: \fIsafeguard.yaml\fP.
Can also be set via the \fBSG_CONFIG_PATH\fP environment variable.
.TP
.BR \--version
Print the version number.
.TP
.BR \--help
Print usage help.
.SS "controller generate Subcommand Options"
.TP
.BR \--output \ PATH
Output path for the whitelist YAML configuration file. Default: \fIdemo-whitelist.yaml\fP.
.TP
.BR \--report \ PATH
Output path for the whitelist JSON report file. Default: \fIdemo-whitelist-report.json\fP.
.TP
.BR \--mode \ MODE
Operational mode for the generated configuration: \fImonitor\fP (log only) or \fIblock\fP (enforce). Default: \fImonitor\fP.
